anv: never place a bo in compressed PAT memory

This is what INTEL_DEBUG=noccs was actually buying, and it is the last of the
brunch-patches/87-arcvm_seccomp.sh workaround: with this patch the wrapper no
longer exports it, and both drivers keep colour compression everywhere else.

Every ARC window rendered as vertical stripe noise with the coarse layout still
recognisable. Established on the target machine (8086:64a0, xe, ChromeOS R149
guest under crosvm) by a three-step A/B, one variable per step. The per-driver
step is possible because ANV and iris are separate shared objects and
`intel_debug` is not an exported dynamic symbol in either, so each honours or
ignores DEBUG_NO_CCS independently without touching the environment:

  1. de-advertising the Xe2 CCS DRM modifiers in both drivers (0003 + 0004)
     reproduces exactly the modifier lists noccs produced -- measured with
     VkDrmFormatModifierPropertiesListEXT and eglQueryDmaBufModifiersEXT
     against the binaries unpacked from the shipped tarball -- and does NOT
     fix it. So the declared layout is not what matters.
  2. ANV alone made to ignore noccs, iris still honouring it: corruption
     comes back. So it is ANV, not iris.
  3. ANV made to ignore noccs everywhere EXCEPT this branch: clean. So it is
     this branch, not isl.c:3902's aux/CCS_E.

What this does not mean: the obvious story -- compressed bytes exported under a
modifier that says nothing about compression, then read as pixels by an
importer -- is ruled out. anv_image_is_pat_compressible() only offers a
compressed memory type to images that are neither external nor DRM-modifier
tiled, so nothing allocated through this branch is ever exported. The bo is
already wrong to the guest's own rendering, and what reaches the window is a
faithful copy of that garbage.

Why compressed PAT memory misbehaves for a VM guest here is not established --
only that it does. The host reproduction environment cannot show it: with no VM
in the picture, compression round-trips cleanly through every test we have
(texcheck, ccscheck, dmabufcheck, glcheck, glexport all pass with it enabled),
which is why three real-machine rounds were needed to find it. A kernel or
platform interaction is the obvious suspect; that is for the upstream report.

Kept: render target compression, fast clears and sampler decompression, in ANV
and in iris. noccs threw all of that away in both drivers -- measured at +50%
to +83% frame time on bandwidth-bound work (venustest/ccsbench.c).

--- a/src/intel/vulkan/anv_device.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/anv_device.c
@@ -1551,8 +1551,44 @@
        * modifiers and enable compression if we can here.
        */
       alloc_flags |= ANV_BO_ALLOC_COMPRESSED;
-   } else if (mem_type->compressed && !INTEL_DEBUG(DEBUG_NO_CCS)) {
-      alloc_flags |= ANV_BO_ALLOC_COMPRESSED;
+   } else if (mem_type->compressed) {
+      /* brunch: deliberately do NOT set ANV_BO_ALLOC_COMPRESSED here.
+       *
+       * A bo placed in compressed PAT memory comes back as noise for
+       * everything an ARCVM guest draws: every ARC window rendered as
+       * vertical stripe noise with the coarse layout still recognisable.
+       * Established on the target machine (8086:64a0, xe, ChromeOS R149
+       * guest) by a three-step A/B, each step a single variable:
+       *
+       *   1. de-advertising the Xe2 CCS DRM modifiers in both drivers
+       *      (mesa-patches/0003 + 0004) reproduces exactly the modifier
+       *      lists INTEL_DEBUG=noccs produced -- and does not fix it, so
+       *      the declared layout is not what matters;
+       *   2. making ANV alone ignore noccs brings the corruption back
+       *      while iris keeps honouring it -> it is ANV, not iris;
+       *   3. making ANV ignore noccs everywhere EXCEPT this branch is
+       *      clean -> it is this branch, not isl.c's aux/CCS_E.
+       *
+       * Note what this does NOT mean. The obvious story -- compressed
+       * bytes exported under a modifier that does not mention them, then
+       * read as pixels -- is ruled out: anv_image_is_pat_compressible()
+       * only offers a compressed memory type to images that are neither
+       * external nor DRM-modifier tiled, so nothing allocated here is
+       * ever exported. The bo is corrupt to the guest's own rendering,
+       * and the correct copy of that garbage is what reaches the window.
+       * Why compressed PAT memory misbehaves for a VM guest on this
+       * kernel is NOT established -- only that it does. The host
+       * reproduction environment cannot show it: with no VM in the
+       * picture, compression round-trips cleanly through every test
+       * (texcheck, ccscheck, dmabufcheck all pass with it enabled).
+       *
+       * This replaces INTEL_DEBUG=noccs, which brunch-patches/
+       * 87-arcvm_seccomp.sh used to export into the crosvm process tree.
+       * noccs also threw away aux surfaces everywhere (isl.c:3902) in
+       * both drivers; steps 2 and 3 show neither of those was load
+       * bearing, so render target compression, fast clears and sampler
+       * decompression all stay, in ANV and in iris.
+       */
    }
 
    /* Anything imported or exported is EXTERNAL */
